        "date": "2026-11-22T07:08:18Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(xtask): name the signal or crash status of a test executable that dies\n\nA direct test executable that a signal killed had no exit code, so the\ngate logged only `exit -1`, with no test output and no panic (#3258).\nThe gate now writes `gate: the test executable stopped: <how>` into the\nstep log and carries it into the step note: the signal and core dump on\nUnix, the known crash statuses on Windows.\n\nThe aborts of #3258 were signal deaths in the GPU tests on hosts with a\nhardware Vulkan driver, before the runners pinned software Vulkan. No\nhost lock is added; docs/decisions/3258-gate-names-the-crash.md has why.\n\nFixes #3258\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
